## QUICK PERMISSIONS

This section provides a simplified overview of the most important permissions and restrictions. The full license below takes precedence over this summary.

### ✅ YOU MAY

* Download the Original Base for free
* Use the Original Base
* Copy the Original Base
* Study and inspect the Original Base
* Modify the Original Base
* Add your own code, features, systems, and functionality
* Create Modified Software
* Create genuine Derivative Projects
* Redistribute the Original Base for free
* Redistribute Modified Software for free
* Commercialize a genuine Derivative Project
* Sell your own original work incorporated into a Derivative Project
* Rebrand a Derivative Project
* Claim copyright over your own original contributions
* Build a commercial product using the Base, provided it qualifies as a genuine Derivative Project

### ❌ YOU MAY NOT

* Sell the Original Base by itself
* Sell an unchanged copy of the Original Base
* Sell a renamed or rebranded copy of the Original Base
* Put the Original Base behind a paywall
* Charge specifically for access to the Original Base
* Claim that the Original Base was created by you
* Remove or conceal Jatos's original attribution
* Sell the Base with only trivial or cosmetic changes
* Use insignificant modifications to circumvent this License
* Present the Original Base as proprietary software owned by you
* Apply a license that removes or contradicts the rights granted by this License
* Imply that your Derivative Project is officially endorsed by Jatos without written permission

**Important:** Adding your own work does not automatically make a project a Derivative Project. The project must contain meaningful original development as described in this License.

# TERMS AND CONDITIONS FOR USE, MODIFICATION, DISTRIBUTION, AND COMMERCIAL USE

## 1. DEFINITIONS

### 1.1 "License"

"License" means these terms and conditions governing the use, reproduction, modification, distribution, and commercialization of the Software.

### 1.2 "Licensor"

"Licensor" means Jatos, the original copyright holder of the Base, or any person expressly authorized by Jatos in writing to grant permissions under this License.

### 1.3 "You" or "Your"

"You" or "Your" means any individual, organization, company, group, or other legal entity exercising rights granted under this License.

### 1.4 "Software"

"Software" means the source code, object code, compiled binaries, scripts, configuration files, documentation, assets, and other materials distributed by the Licensor under this License.

### 1.5 "Base"

"Base" means the Original Software and its components as distributed by the Licensor and intended to serve as a foundation, framework, starting point, template, or development base for other projects.

### 1.6 "Original Software"

"Original Software" means the Software as originally published and distributed by the Licensor.

### 1.7 "Modification"

"Modification" means any addition, deletion, alteration, adaptation, rewrite, replacement, extension, or other change made to the Original Software.

### 1.8 "Modified Software"

"Modified Software" means Software containing one or more Modifications.

### 1.9 "Derivative Project"

"Derivative Project" means a project based upon or incorporating the Base that contains substantial original functionality, features, systems, code, assets, design, or other original creative work created by You or Your contributors.

### 1.10 "Original Base"

"Original Base" means the Base itself, including substantially unchanged copies, lightly modified copies, renamed copies, rebranded copies, or other distributions where the primary value and functionality of the distributed product remain substantially derived from the Original Software.

### 1.11 "Commercial Use"

"Commercial Use" means any use intended to generate monetary or commercial benefit, including selling software, subscriptions, services, access, licenses, or other products.

Commercial Use is permitted under this License only when the Software forms part of a genuine Derivative Project as defined by this License.

### 1.12 "Attribution Notice"

"Attribution Notice" means the copyright and author acknowledgment identifying Jatos as the original creator of the Base.

